      <activity id="7613092f-6228-55b4-9d89-ab6228a23222" activityNameId="6a44446a-953f-5fc0-ac09-71f27473a4bf" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Direct air capture system, sorbent-based, 100ktCO2</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Direct air capture system, sorbent-based, 100ktCO2
For the sorbent system, the LCI data are collected from the work of Deutz and Bardow based on the Climeworks system. The LCI data represent a plant with an annual capacity of 100 kt CO2/year and a lifetime of 20 years. Source: Qiu, Y., Lamers, P., Daioglou, V. et al. Environmental trade-offs of direct air capture technologies in climate change mitigation toward 2100. Nat Commun 13, 3635 (2022). https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-022-31146-1

 UUID: 7484b270-e065-46c4-9759-89c4d046dc52
Location: 
Technology: 
Time period: 
Production volume: 
Sampling: Sampling procedure: Literature data
Extrapolations: 
Uncertainty adjustments: 
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_7484b270-e065-46c4-9759-89c4d046dc52.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
